From: vyos-ls1046a-build CI <ci@local>
Date: Mon, 05 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fman_pcd: lead VLAN ehash records with 04 + STRIP_ETH_HDR (fixes VLAN translate)

The 0209 inline VLAN records carried `12 21 42 41 01` without the
vendor's STRIP_ETH_HDR (0x11). On silicon (.185, 2026-10-05) frames
then left with the ingress tag unchanged: same length, VID 10 instead
of 20. STRIP and INSERT run against a frame that still starts at the
DA, and only INSERT_L2's in-place MAC/EtherType rewrite takes effect.

Adding 0x11 as the FIRST opcode wedges the RX port at once (all hits
stop, then the whole port goes RX-deaf; only a cold power-cycle
recovers). Reproduced twice, and still with the vendor RX-port
settings applied (rim/rpso 96 B headroom, RFENE 0x22, RCMNE 0x0e, params
misc bit 30), so port config is not the factor.

Live record bisection on the same board, rewriting one active record
and keeping traffic paused across the write:
  05 04 11 12 21 42 41 01 (vendor-exact) -> VID 20, line rate, no wedge
  04 11 12 21 42 41 01                   -> VID 20, line rate, no wedge
  05 11 12 21 42 41 01                   -> VID 20, line rate, no wedge
  11 12 21 42 41 01                      -> RX-deaf
So 0x11 must not be opcode 0. The vendor always has PREEMPTIVE_CHECKS and
UPDATE_ETH_RX_STATS in front of it (cdx_ehash.c fill_actions()).

Fix: for any record with a VLAN pop/push, emit UPDATE_ETH_RX_STATS
(0x04, 4 B param, stats_ptr 0 = no stats, as the vendor writes it
without INCLUDE_ETHER_IFSTATS) and then STRIP_ETH_HDR (0x11, no param)
ahead of the VLAN ops. Records without VLAN edits stay byte-identical.

Silicon-validated: VLAN->VLAN translate (pop+push). Push-only and pop-only
records take the same prefix but are not yet validated on silicon.
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd.c
index 2fdf156..14c5592 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd.c
@@ -2359,6 +2359,26 @@ static int fman_pcd_ehash_add_key(struct fman_pcd_ehash_table *t,
 			 * opcode so later params land after it; ttl_param_off (not
 			 * param_off) is threaded through so the no-VLAN case stays
 			 * byte-identical. */
+			/* Vendor fill_actions() rebuilds L2 for any VLAN edit with
+			 * STRIP_ETH_HDR (0x11) ahead of the VLAN ops, and always
+			 * has PREEMPTIVE_CHECKS/UPDATE_ETH_RX_STATS in front of it.
+			 * On 210.10.1 0x11 must NOT be the first opcode: as opcode 0
+			 * it wedges the RX port (RX-deaf, cold power-cycle only);
+			 * with any opcode before it the VLAN translate executes
+			 * (SILICON 2026-10-05, .185: 04/05/both prefixes each gave
+			 * VID 10 -> 20 at line rate). Without 0x11 at all the frame
+			 * leaves with the ingress tag unchanged. Lead with
+			 * UPDATE_ETH_RX_STATS (0x04), stats_ptr 0 = no stats. */
+			#define FMAN_EHASH_OPC_UPDATE_ETH_RX_STATS	0x04
+			#define FMAN_EHASH_OPC_STRIP_ETH_HDR		0x11
+			if (vlan && (vlan->flags &
+				     (FMAN_PCD_VLANF_POP | FMAN_PCD_VLANF_PUSH))) {
+				r[opc_off + oi++] = FMAN_EHASH_OPC_UPDATE_ETH_RX_STATS;
+				*(__be32 *)(r + param_off) = cpu_to_be32(0);
+				param_off += 4;
+				ttl_param_off = param_off;
+				r[opc_off + oi++] = FMAN_EHASH_OPC_STRIP_ETH_HDR;
+			}
 			if (vlan_pop) {
 				r[opc_off + oi++] = FMAN_EHASH_OPC_STRIP_ALL_VLAN;
 				*(__be16 *)(r + param_off + 0) =
